<!--Post: 9422--><!--Time: 1109516391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 6:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I figured I&#39;d start a thread about the wife of the accused serial killer aka &#34;BTK.&#34;  I didn&#39;t see it anywhere else so if it&#39;s already been done, I apologize.  We&#39;ve heard a lot about BTK&#39;s daughter, Kerri, and rightfully so.  But I haven&#39;t heard much about his wife, Paula. <BR> <BR>Does anyone know anything about her?  Does she work?  What she is like?  I just can&#39;t imagine being married to someone for years, sleeping next to them, having children with them only to find out that person is a notorious serial killer!  I wonder what is going on in her head.  Like most wives in these situations, I&#39;m sure it&#39;s one of disbelief.  Her world is being turned upside down.  She,too, is another victim &#40;as well as his children&#41;.  I wonder if she ever suspected him??  <BR> <BR>Thoughts?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9422-->
<!--Post: 9424--><!--Time: 1109518837-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9424"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 7:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ive been trying to imagine how his wife would feel. <BR>Best guess, awful. depressed. angry. shock, disblief, confused. <BR> <BR>Im still trying to figure out the order of events. I forget where I heard about getting this guy on video tape making a &#42;drop&#42; at a home depot? And his daughter giving a blood sample. Did le already have a bead on him? Then they asked for a sample? <BR>or vice versa?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9424-->
<!--Post: 9515--><!--Time: 1109543375-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9515"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 2:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Supposedly the daughter contacted police on or about the 12th. She initiated the contact. The drop we didn&#39;t hear about was on Monday or Tuesday evening, and both he and his vehicle were shown on the Home Depot tapes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9515-->
<!--Post: 9646--><!--Time: 1109577492-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9646"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 11:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One nieghbor who absolutely hated Dennis Rader and tried three times to challenge him to a fight described Rader&#39;s wife as a wonderful woman who he and all the nieghbors liked a lot. Go figure. Opposites attract.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9646-->
<!--Post: 9655--><!--Time: 1109580953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 12:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Pastor of their Church described her as &#34;soft spoken&#34; during his interview on KAKE News...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9655-->
<!--Post: 9665--><!--Time: 1109583786-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9665"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:zodiacfiles@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ed_neil<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ed_neil<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 1:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s keep speculation/rumors/chat in general about Rader&#39;s family to a minimum, other than what&#39;s been mentioned in the various news media.  BTK is about Dennis Lynn Rader, not his family.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9665-->
<!--Post: 9732--><!--Time: 1109620407-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 11:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I find it very hard to believe that if a man is married and he is out murdering people that a spouse would not pick up on his behavior.  I mean seriously, us women have a instinct that tell us when something is up...if my husband was to come home grouchy, fidgety, or unusually happy and giddy...trust me I would know something was up.  I mean the man stabbed people...and we all know that no matter how careful you are...you cannot get rid of all the blood, she had to have noticed something on his shoes, his vehicle, or on a piece of clothing etc...it just does not make sense that she did not pick up on any irregularities in his behavior.  Yes, he was a control freak, and it is possible that deep down inside she was terrified of him.  I don&#39;t know what to think about her, anyway just rambling here so I thought I would post it and see how other women are analyzing the wife in their own minds and perspective.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9732-->
<!--Post: 9737--><!--Time: 1109621951-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 12:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have to agree with Tornado <BR> <BR>While I feel for her and her children I also cannot help but feel that she had to have at least suspected <i>something</i> in all these years. As Tornado said, if my husband came home acting different, I would think something was up. But lets say Dennis always acted the same at home. I would be extremely suspicous of his stashes!!! And we know he had them. Be it out in his little shed or whatever. If he had a place that he absolutely would not let anyone near, I would have to know what the hell it was.........evenually! Give me a break. Either this woman is catatonic or she had to have known her little hubby was up to no good. I dont think anyone can hide their true personality from family for that many years. No way<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9737-->
<!--Post: 9754--><!--Time: 1109629677-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9754"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 2:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In response to Ed_Neil&#39;s posting, I can only say that BTK is so much more than just Dennis Rader - it extends to his victims, his family, the media, the citizens of Wichita and the surrounding areas, LE, the media and people around the country who are interested in this case.  I am not here to start rumors and talk badly about his family nor do I feel anyone else is here to do that.   <BR> <BR>However, if people want to have &#34;adult&#34; conversations about his family, and do so respectfully, then I think we should be able to just that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9754-->
<!--Post: 9779--><!--Time: 1109637138-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9779"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bojo<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bojo<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->So women know all.  How do you explain husbands cheating on thier wives and the wives never knowing?  Remember we&#39;re not talking about a normal perosn here.  We&#39;re talking about a cold, sick, preverted killer. This is not a guy you can&#39;t lump in with the masses.  He&#39;s a freak, even amoung seriel killers he&#39;s a freak. I can easily see him hiding his actions.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9779-->
<!--Post: 9782--><!--Time: 1109637587-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 4:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well Bojo all I can say to that is....if my husband was in a building on my property outside of my house at 1 or 2 AM in the morning...trust me, the next day while he was gone...I would get in that building and I would know what it was that he was doing or watching.  It was reported by a neighbor that he spent a lot of late nights in his little building, now to say that his wife knew nothing of it....I&#39;m sorry I just don&#39;t buy it...she knew of it his little night time visits to his building...she may not have ever entered his domain because of orders he barked out to her, but the normal woman would have found a way to get in that building just to see what had his attention in the wee hours of the morning.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9782-->
<!--Post: 9787--><!--Time: 1109638962-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9787"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bojo<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bojo<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 5:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tornado,  I hear ya.  And I really didn&#39;t mean to make my post so combative.  Sorry. <BR> <BR>I have a friend that works in his &#34;shop&#34; to all hours.  He&#39;s been doing it for years.  His wife would not find it odd that he was playing in the garage, tool shed, what ever you want to call it.  As a matter of fact, I think she would find it strange if he didn&#39;t.  I think it&#39;s obvious that this guy knew how to fit in.  Casting a bad light on the wife is, in my opinion, wrong.  His whole church bought his story.  His co-workers bought it.  If rumors are true, the police bought it.  &#40;He, supposedly, was questioned early in the investigation and agian in the 80&#39;s&#41;   <BR> <BR>My main point is this guy fit in.  Implicating or inferring his family is wrong.  JMHO<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9787-->
<!--Post: 9796--><!--Time: 1109644634-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9796"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I also know of a woman whose husband spends all of his free time in his &#34;shop&#34; &#40;aka the garage&#41;, to the point where he installed a TV in there.  It&#39;s definitely not an ideal or healthy marriage, but they stay together because of their religious beliefs and their daughter.  Perhaps the same can be said of Dennis and Paula Rader. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9796-->
<!--Post: 9797--><!--Time: 1109644972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9797"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 28, 2005 - 6:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bojo...I was just stating things from a woman&#39;s point of view in regards to suspicious things he did and how a spouse would notice if their significant other was acting abnormal or out of character was all.  Have a great night <IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9797-->
<!--Post: 9873--><!--Time: 1109672635-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9873"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 2:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that we should be able to discuss this woman in the context that she was there. On the other hand I say that knowing that she is not going to read these posts. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m thinking &#40;this is hypothetical&#41; that if she did find out she would be so terrified that she might block it from her consciousness, thinking subconsciously that if she so much thought it he would know and kill her. <BR> <BR>There might be a new phenomenon emerge from this trial similar to &#34;Battered Wife Syndrome&#34;. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9873-->
<!--Post: 10029--><!--Time: 1109730656-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10029"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 6:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B- I agree. From all that I know of Mrs.R, she was a happy bubbly nice lady. But who knows what happened behind closed doors. Still, how on earth could she have not known?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
