<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10084"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 10:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree.  Some people&#39;s hubbies are pack rats after all.  I mean even my aunt&#39;s husband wanted to buy land one time just to store all his &#34;stuff&#34; there that didn&#39;t fit into their two-car garage.  I think that it&#39;s even likely that at some point in their lives, she even told family about Dennis&#39; shed and closet where he kept all his &#34;manly&#34; tools and other things.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
